0101           JOB  PCIR - PRINT CAPR INDEX REPORTS - NOV 18, 1964         PCIR 
0102           CTL  431                                                    PCIR 
0103 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0104 *  PROGRAMMERS - DON MILLER AND DONNA MONTGOMERY                      PCIR 
0105 *                                                                     PCIR 
0106 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0107 * THE DETAIL INPUT FOR BOTH REPORTS IS READ FROM TAPE 1.              PCIR 
0108 * THE SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION CARD TABLE INPUT IS PLACED DIRECTLY    PCIR 
0109 *BEHIND THE CONTROL CARD.                                             PCIR 
0110 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0111 * THIS PROGRAM PREPARES TWO PRINTED REPORTS- ON LINE                  PCIR 
0112 *     1. CAPR - KEYWORD INDEX                                         PCIR 
0113 *     2. CAPR - SUBJECT CODE INDEX                                    PCIR 
0114 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0115 *SENSE SWITCHES-                                                      PCIR 
0116 *     IO - ALWAYS ON                                                  PCIR 
0117 *     A  - ALWAYS ON                                                  PCIR 
0118 *     B  - NOT USED                                                   PCIR 
0119 *     C  - NOT USED                                                   PCIR 
0120 *     D  - NOT USED                                                   PCIR 
0121 *     E  - USED WITH READ HEADER LABEL HALTS 566, 567 AND 568.        PCIR 
0121B*          ON - TO CONTINUE PROCESSING THE FIRST DATA RECORD ON       PCIR 
0121C*               THE REEL.                                             PCIR 
0121D*          OFF - TO RETURN TO READ AND CHECK THE HEADER LABEL.        PCIR 
0122 *     F  - USED WITH HALT 522- READ TRAILER ERROR CONDITION.          PCIR 
0123 *          SEE HALT 522.                                              PCIR 
0124 *     G  - TURNED ON TO BRANCH AROUND READ TRAILER LABEL              PCIR 
0125 *          ERRORS AT HALTS 525, 526, AND 527.                         PCIR 
0126 *                                                                     PCIR 
0127 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0128 * HALTS AND ACTION                                                    PCIR 
0129 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0130 *                                                                     PCIR 
0131 *     HALT PROG.  CAUSE AND+OR                                        PCIR 
0132 *     NO.  LABEL  ACTION TO TAKE                                      PCIR 
0133 *     ---- -----  --------------                                      PCIR 
0134 *     511  I14J7  TAPE 1 INPUT END OF REEL.  MOUNT NEXT INPUT REEL    PCIR 
0135 *                 AND PRESS START                                     PCIR 
0136 *     522  I19    CAUSED BY READ ERROR CONDITION WHEN READING         PCIR 
0137 *                 TRAILER LABEL.                                      PCIR 
0137B*                 NOTE - IF THE SORTED INDEX RECORDS FILE WAS         PCIR 
0137C*                 SORTED ON A 1401 USING THE SORT 01 PROGRAM,         PCIR 
0137D*                 THIS FILE WILL NOT HAVE TRAILER LABELS, HENCE       PCIR 
0137E*                 THIS HALT IS APT TO OCCUR.                          PCIR 
0137K*                  3 ACTIONS PROVIDED -                               PCIR 
0138 *                   1. SENSE SW F ON, PRESS START TO TRY TO READ      PCIR 
0139 *                      TRAILER NINE MORE TIMES.                       PCIR 
0140 *                   2. SENSE SW F OFF AND G ON, PRESS START TO GO     PCIR 
0141 *                      TO END OF JOB ROUTINE IF IT IS LAST REEL       PCIR 
0142 *                      OF INPUT.                                      PCIR 
0143 *                   3. SENSE SW F AND G OFF, PRESS START TO GO TO     PCIR 
0144 *                      END OF REEL ROUTINE IF IT IS NOT THE LAST      PCIR 
0145 *                      REEL OF INPUT.                                 PCIR 
0146 *     525  I25    NO TRAILER LABEL - THAT IS THE REEL WAS ENDED       PCIR 
0147 *                 BY 2 SUCCESSIVE TAPE MARKS.                         PCIR 
0148 *                 2 ACTIONS AVAILABLE-                                PCIR 
0149 *                   1. SENSE SW G ON, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF     PCIR 
0150 *                      JOB IF IT IS LAST REEL OF INPUT.               PCIR 
0151 *                   2. SENSE SW G OFF, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF    PCIR 
0152 *                      REEL ROUTINE IF IT IS NOT LAST REEL OF INPUT   PCIR 
0153 *     526  I26    IMPROPER TRAILER LABEL, DID NOT HAVE 1EO IN 1ST     PCIR 
0154 *                 3 POSITIONS.                                        PCIR 
0154B*                 NOTE - IF THE SORTED INDEX RECORDS FILE WAS         PCIR 
0154C*                 SORTED ON A 1401 USING THE SORT 01 PROGRAM,         PCIR 
0154D*                 THIS FILE WILL NOT HAVE TRAILER LABELS, HENCE       PCIR 
0154E*                 THIS HALT IS APT TO OCCUR.                          PCIR 
0155 *                 2 ACTIONS AVAILABLE-                                PCIR 
0156 *                   1. SENSE SW G ON, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF     PCIR 
0157 *                      JOB IF IT IS LAST REEL OF INPUT.               PCIR 
0158 *                   2. SENSE SW G OFF, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF    PCIR 
0159 *                      REEL ROUTINE IF IT IS NOT LAST REEL OF INPUT   PCIR 
0160 *     527  I27    TRAILER LABEL AND PROGRAM BLOCK COUNT DO NOT        PCIR 
0161 *                 AGREE.                                              PCIR 
0162 *                 2 ACTIONS AVAILABLE-                                PCIR 
0163 *                   1. SENSE SW G ON, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF     PCIR 
0164 *                      JOB IF IT IS LAST REEL OF INPUT.               PCIR 
0165 *                   2. SENSE SW G OFF, PRESS START TO GO TO END OF    PCIR 
0166 *                      REEL ROUTINE IF IT IS NOT LAST REEL OF INPUT   PCIR 
0167 *     531  I11    WRONG LENGTH RECORD LOCKED HALT.  TAKE CORE DUMP,   PCIR 
0168 *                 BACKSPACE TAPE 2 RECORDS AND TAKE TAPE DUMP OF      PCIR 
0169 *                 A FEW RECORDS. ABANDON JOB.                         PCIR 
0169B*     566  H12    THE FIRST RECORD ON THE SIR INPUT TAPE IS NOT A     PCIR 
0169C*                 HEADER LABEL - DOES NOT HAVE 1HDR IN THE FIRST      PCIR 
0169D*                 FOUR POSITIONS. TAKE ANY OF THESE 3 ACTIONS-        PCIR 
0169E*                1. IF THIS CONDITION IS EXPECTED, THAT IS THE SORT   PCIR 
0169F*                 USED FOR THE SCIR PROCESSING DROPS THE MIR HEADER   PCIR 
0169G*                 LABEL PROVIDED BY PDAP AND DOES NOT REPLACE IT      PCIR 
0169H*                 WITH AN SIR HEADER LABEL, THEN SET SENSE SWITCH     PCIR 
0169I*                 E ON AND PRESS START. THE PROGRAM WILL BACKSPACE    PCIR 
0169J*                 THE TAPE EXPECTING THE FIRST RECORD TO BE A DATA    PCIR 
0169K*                 RECORD AND CONTINUE PROCESSING.                     PCIR 
0169L*                2. IF A HEADER LABEL IS EXPECTED, AN IMPROPER REEL   PCIR 
0169M*                 HAS BEEN MOUNTED. IF PROPER REEL CAN BE LOCATED,    PCIR 
0169N*                 MOUNT IT, SET SENSE SWITCH E OFF AND PRESS START.   PCIR 
0169O*                 THE PROGRAM WILL RETURN TO READ THE HEADER LABEL.   PCIR 
0169S*                3. ANY OTHER CONDITION NOT COVERED BY PARAGRAPHS     PCIR 
0169T*                 1 AND 2 ABOVE, TAKE DIAGNOSTIC ACTION AND           PCIR 
0169U*                 ABANDON JOB.                                        PCIR 
0170A*     567  H13    THE HEADER LABEL ON THE SORTED INDEX RECORDS TAPE   PCIR 
0170B*                 DOES NOT HAVE SIR AS THE HEADER LABEL ID.           PCIR 
0170C*                  NOTE THAT THIS CONDITION MAY EXIST IF THE          PCIR 
0170D*                  SORTED INDEX RECORDS FILE WAS SORTED ON A 1401     PCIR 
0170E*                  USING THE SORT 01 PROGRAM WHICH DID NOT INCLUDE    PCIR 
0170F*                  AN OUTPUT HEADER LABEL CARD WITH THE CONTROL       PCIR 
0170G*                  CARD.                                              PCIR 
0170K*                     3 ACTIONS PROVIDED -                            PCIR 
0170L*                  1. IF THIS CONDITION IS EXPECTED, SET SENSE        PCIR 
0170M*                   SWITCH E ON AND PRESS START TO CONTINUE           PCIR 
0170N*                   PROCESSING WITH THE NEXT TAPE RECORD.             PCIR 
0170O*                  2. IF THIS CONDITION IS NOT EXPECTED AN IMPROPER   PCIR 
0170P*                   REEL HAS BEEN MOUNTED. MOUNT THE PROPER REEL,     PCIR 
0170Q*                   SET SENSE SWITCH E OFF AND PRESS START. THE       PCIR 
0170R*                   PROGRAM WILL RETURN TO READ THE HEADER LABEL.     PCIR 
0170S*                3. ANY OTHER CONDITION NOT COVERED BY PARAGRAPHS     PCIR 
0170T*                 1 AND 2 ABOVE, TAKE DIAGNOSTIC ACTION AND           PCIR 
0170U*                 ABANDON JOB.                                        PCIR 
0171A*     568  H14    THE HEADER LABEL ON THE SORTED INDEX RECORDS TAPE   PCIR 
0171B*                 DOES HAVE SIR AS AN ID, BUT HAS AN IMPROPER REEL    PCIR 
0171C*                 SEQUENCE NUMBER.                                    PCIR 
0171D*                NOTE THAT THIS CONDITION MAY EXIST IF THIS IS        PCIR 
0171E*                THE SECOND THRU FINAL REEL PRODUCED BY A 1401        PCIR 
0171F*                PROCESSING USING THE SORT 01 PROGRAM.                PCIR 
0171J*                     3 ACTIONS PROVIDED -                            PCIR 
0171K*                  1. IF THIS CONDITION IS EXPECTED, SET SENSE        PCIR 
0171L*                   SWITCH E ON AND PRESS START TO CONTINUE           PCIR 
0171M*                   PROCESSING WITH THE NEXT TAPE RECORD.             PCIR 
0171N*                  2. IF THIS CONDITION IS NOT EXPECTED AN IMPROPER   PCIR 
0171O*                   REEL HAS BEEN MOUNTED. MOUNT THE PROPER REEL,     PCIR 
0171P*                   SET SENSE SWITCH E OFF AND PRESS START. THE       PCIR 
0171Q*                   PROGRAM WILL RETURN TO READ THE HEADER LABEL.     PCIR 
0171S*                3. ANY OTHER CONDITION NOT COVERED BY PARAGRAPHS     PCIR 
0171T*                 1 AND 2 ABOVE, TAKE DIAGNOSTIC ACTION AND           PCIR 
0171U*                 ABANDON JOB.                                        PCIR 
0172 *     571  I08    READ ERROR CONDITION ON TAPE 1. THE PROGRAM HAS     PCIR 
0173 *                 TRIED 9 TIMES TO READ THE RECORD BUT THE ERROR      PCIR 
0174 *                 PERSISTS.  PRESS START TO TRY 9 MORE TIMES OR       PCIR 
0175 *                 TAKE DIAGNOSTIC ACTION AND ABANDON JOB.             PCIR 
0176 *     578  H06    READ ERROR ENCOUNTERED WHEN READING HEADER LABEL    PCIR 
0176B*                 ON SIR FILE, TAPE 1.  THE PROGRAM HAS TRIED 9       PCIR 
0176C*                 TIMES TO READ THE LABEL.                            PCIR 
0176D*                   CHECK FOR PROPER TAPE.                            PCIR 
0176E*                   PRESS START TO TRY 9 MORE TIMES.                  PCIR 
0179G*     579  H15    A TAPE MARK WAS THE FIRST RECORD READ ON THE SIR    PCIR 
0179H*                 INPUT TAPE. MOUNT CORRECT REEL AND PRESS START      PCIR 
0179I*                 TO CONTINUE PROCESSING.                             PCIR 
0180 *     608  B18    SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE CARDS OUT OF         PCIR 
0181 *                 SEQUENCE. RESEQUENCE TABLE CARDS AND RESTART JOB.   PCIR 
0182 *     609  B33    INPUT ON TAPE 1 OUT OF SEQUENCE.  TAKE DIAGNOSTIC   PCIR 
0183 *                 ACTION AND ABANDON JOB.                             PCIR 
0184 *     800  A03    IMPROPER CONTROL CARD REPORT DATE. RUN CARDS OUT    PCIR 
0185 *                 WITH NON PROCESS RUN-OUT READ KEY. CORRECT          PCIR 
0186 *                 CONTROL CARD AND PLACE CONTROL CARD FOLLOWED BY     PCIR 
0187 *                 THE SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE IN THE READ      PCIR 
0188 *                 HOPPER AND PRESS START.                             PCIR 
0189 *     801  B04    TYPE RECORD UNKNOWN LOCKED HALT. TAKE DIAGNOSTIC    PCIR 
0190 *                 ACTION AND ABANDON JOB.                             PCIR 
0191 *     999  I22    END OF JOB.                                         PCIR 
0192 *                                                                     PCIR 
0193 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0194 *   CONTROL CARD -INPUT VIA CARD READER                               PCIR 
0195 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0196           EQU  17  6-17, REPORT TITLE DATE                            PCIR 
0197 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0198 * SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTIONS - INPUT VIA CARD READER                   PCIR 
0199 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0200           EQU  3    1-3, SUBJECT CODE                                 PCIR 
0201           EQU  72  4-72, SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION                     PCIR 
0202 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0203 * REPORT TITLE AREA - THE AREA IS USED FOR BOTH REPORTS-              PCIR 
0204 * MODIFIED BETWEEN REPORTS.                                           PCIR 
0205 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0206 TITLE     EQU  *+1                                                    PCIR 
0207 RPTNO     DCW  'KW      '                                             PCIR 
0208           DC   =6                                                     PCIR 
0209 DATE      DCW  =12                DATE OF RUN                         PCIR 
0210           DC   =8                                                     PCIR 
0211 TNM       DC   'CAPR - KEYWORD PERMUTED INDEX'                        PCIR 
0212           DC   =7                                                     PCIR 
0213           DC   'PAGE'                                                 PCIR 
0214           DCW  '⯒'  GM                                                PCIR 
0215 PGCT      DCW  '    '                                                 PCIR 
0216           DC   '.00'                                                  PCIR 
0217 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0218 * KEYWORD INDEX DETAIL PRINT LINE                                     PCIR 
0219 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0220 DET1      DA   1X83,G                                                 PCIR 
0221 SERCH1         2,64      KEYWORDS                                     PCIR 
0222 STC1           74,76     SUBMITTERS INSTALLATION CODE                 PCIR 
0223 ID1            79,83     PROGRAM I.D.                                 PCIR 
0224 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0225 * SUBJECT CODE  GROUP DESCRIPTION PRINT LINE                          PCIR 
0226 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0227 SUBJ2     DA   1X76,G                                                 PCIR 
0228 SUB2           2,4       SUBJECT CODE                                 PCIR 
0229 SUBID2         7,75      SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION                     PCIR 
0230 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0231 * SUBJECT CODE DETAIL PRINT LINE                                      PCIR 
0232 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0233 DET2      DA   1X83,G                                                 PCIR 
0234 STC2           11,13     SUBMITTERS INSTALLATION CODE                 PCIR 
0235 ID2            16,20     PROGRAM I.D.                                 PCIR 
0236 TITLE2         27,83     PROGRAM TITLE                                PCIR 
0237 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0238 * DETAIL INPUT AREA FROM TAPE 1-                                      PCIR 
0239 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0240 INPUT     DA   1X84,G,X1                                              PCIR 
0241 CTL            1,6       SHARE CONTROL WORD - ALWAYS C00078           PCIR 
0242                7         ALWAYS AN *.                                 PCIR 
0243 TYPE           8,8       1 FOR KEYWORD.      2 FOR SUBJECT CODE.      PCIR 
0244 INP11          11                           2-SUBJECT CODE            PCIR 
0245 INP14          14                           2-INSTALLATION CODE       PCIR 
0246 INP19          19                           2-PROGRAM I.D             PCIR 
0247 INP76          76                           2-PROGRAM TITLE           PCIR 
0248 INP71          71       1-SEARCH KEYS                                 PCIR 
0249 INP74          74       1-INSTALLATION CODE                           PCIR 
0250 INP79          79       1-PROGRAM I.D.                                PCIR 
0251 INP84          84       1-RECORD MARK       2-RECORD MARK             PCIR 
0252 GM        DCW  '⯒'  GM                                                PCIR 
0253 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0254 * CONSTANTS, COUNTERS, ETC.                                           PCIR 
0255 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0256 KWREC     DCW  =6        KEYWORD INPUT RECORD COUNT.                  PCIR 
0257 SIREC     DCW  =6        SUBJECT CODE DETAIL INPUT RECORD COUNT.      PCIR 
0258 RECNT     DCW  =6        TOTAL OF KEYWORD AND SUBJECT CODE DETAIL     PCIR 
0259 *                        INPUT COUNT RECEIVED FROM SCIR.              PCIR 
0260 SCDCT     DCW  =6        SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE CARD COUNT.   PCIR 
0261 LINEPA    DCW  '40'      NUMBER OF BODY LINES PER PAGE DESIRED.       PCIR 
0262 *                          COMPARED TO LINECT FOR PAGE EJECTION.      PCIR 
0262A*                         IF THE CONSTANT FOR LINEPA IS CHANGED,      PCIR 
0262B*                         THE CONSTANT FOR LINECT MUST BE CHANGED     PCIR 
0262C*                         ACCORDINGLY IN ORDER TO FORCE THE TITLE     PCIR 
0262D*                         LINE TO PRINT ON THE 1ST PAGE OF THE        PCIR 
0262E*                         REPORT AND TO INSURE PROPER HANDLING        PCIR 
0262F*                         OF THE 1ST PAGE.                            PCIR 
0263 LINECT    DCW  '40'      NUMBER OF BODY LINES ALREADY USED FOR        PCIR 
0263A*                          CURRENT PAGE.                              PCIR 
0264 BLANKS    DA   1X40                                                   PCIR 
0265 89        DCW  '000'                                                  PCIR 
0266 X1        EQU  89                                                     PCIR 
0267 XXXX      EQU  0                                                      PCIR 
0268 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0269 * HOUSEKEEPING  ROUTINE                                               PCIR 
0270 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0271 A01       R                       READ CONTROL CARD                   PCIR 
0272           SS   1                                                      PCIR 
0273           SW   1                                                      PCIR 
0274           C    17,BLANKS+11        IS THERE A REPORT DATE             PCIR 
0274C          BE   A03                                                    PCIR 
0275           BCE  A04,1,              1ST COL. OF CONTROL CARD SHOULD    PCIR 
0275C*                                  BE BLANK, AND THE 1ST COL. OF      PCIR 
0275E*                                  THE SUBJ. CODE CARDS WILL NOT.     PCIR 
0276 A03       NOP  800       NO DATE CARD HALT                            PCIR 
0277           H                                                           PCIR 
0278           B    A01                                                    PCIR 
0279 A04       MLC  17,DATE     CONTROL CARD DATE TO REPORT TITLE AREA.    PCIR 
0280           B    H01                CHECK HEADER LABEL ON INPUT         PCIR 
0281           MLC  '      ',6    PREPARE CARD AREA FOR SUBJECT            PCIR 
0282           SW   4              CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE.                 PCIR 
0283           SBR  I99+3,B02  SET GET DETAIL INPUT RTE TO RETURN TO B02   PCIR 
0284           B    I05       GET DETAIL INPUT.                            PCIR 
0285 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0286 *    MAIN ROUTINE                                                     PCIR 
0287 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0288 B01       B    I01                GET INPUT RECORD                    PCIR 
0289 B02       BCE  B35,TYPE,1         KEYWORD RECORD                      PCIR 
0290 B03       BCE  B05,TYPE,2    1ST TIME BR TO B05-ALL OTHER TIMES B14   PCIR 
0291 B04       NOP  801                                                    PCIR 
0292           H                  TYPE RECORD UNKNOWN HALT                 PCIR 
0293           B    B04                                                    PCIR 
0294 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0295 *  MAIN ROUTINE - SUBJECT CODE PROCESSING                             PCIR 
0296 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0297 B05       SBR  B03+3,B14                                              PCIR 
0298           BCE  B12,PGCT,   BR IF THERE WAS NO KEYWORD REPORT.         PCIR 
0299 * WIND UP KEYWORD INDEX REPORT AND HOUSEKEEP FOR SUBJECT CODE INDEX   PCIR 
0300           CC   1                  SKIP TO NEW PAGE                    PCIR 
0301           MLC  'KEYWORD DETAIL INPUT RECORDS',236                     PCIR 
0302           MCS  KWREC,207                                              PCIR 
0303           W                       PRINT RECORD COUNT                  PCIR 
0304           CS   299                CLEAR PRINT AREA                    PCIR 
0305           MLC  LINEPA,LINECT   SET FOR NEW PAGE.                      PCIR 
0306           MLC  '    ',PGCT                                            PCIR 
0307 B12       MLC  'SI',RPTNO-6                                           PCIR 
0308           MLC  'SUBJECT CODE INDEX    ',TNM                           PCIR 
0309 * BUILD SUBJECT CODE DETAIL PRINT LINE.                               PCIR 
0310 B14       MLC  INP14,STC2     INSTALLATION CODE                       PCIR 
0311           MLC  INP19,ID2      PROGRAM I.D.                            PCIR 
0312           MLC  INP76,TITLE2    PROGRAM  TITLE                         PCIR 
0313 * HAS SUBJECT CODE CHANGED.                                           PCIR 
0314 B15       C    INP11,SUB2                                             PCIR 
0315           BE   B29                                                    PCIR 
0316           BH   B33            INPUT OUT OF SEQUENCE                   PCIR 
0317 * GET SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION FROM CARD TABLE                        PCIR 
0318 B17       C    INP11,3   COMPARE IP SUBJ CODE TO TABLE CARD.          PCIR 
0319 B17SW     BH   B32                TABLE CARD MISSING- THIS SWITCH     PCIR 
0320 *                               SET TO AN UNCONDITIONAL BRANCH WHEN   PCIR 
0321 *                               ALL TABLE CARDS HAVE BEEN READ.       PCIR 
0322           BE   B23                TABLE CARD MATCHES                  PCIR 
0323           BLC  B19       NO MORE TABLE CARDS.                         PCIR 
0324           R                       READ TABLE CARD                     PCIR 
0325           SS   1                                                      PCIR 
0326           A    *-6,SCDCT   ADD 1 TO SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE    PCIR 
0327 *                           CARD COUNT.                               PCIR 
0328           C    SUB2,3                                                 PCIR 
0329           BL   B18       TABLE OUT OF SEQUENCE                        PCIR 
0330           B    B17                                                    PCIR 
0331 * SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION TABLE OUT OF SEQUENCE - RESTART JOB.       PCIR 
0332 B18       NOP  608                                                    PCIR 
0333           H                                                           PCIR 
0334           B    B18                                                    PCIR 
0335 * NO MORE TABLE CARDS                                                 PCIR 
0336 B19       SW   B17SW+4   SET B17SW TO AN UNCONDITIONAL BRANCH.        PCIR 
0337           B    B32                                                    PCIR 
0338 *BUILD SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION LINE FROM TABLE CARD.                 PCIR 
0339 B23       MLC  INP11,SUB2     SUBJECT CODE AND DESCRIPTION            PCIR 
0340           MLC  72,SUBID2       TO PRINT AREA.                         PCIR 
0341 * SET PRINT ROUTINE TO PRINT SUBJECT CODE DESCRIPTION LINE.           PCIR 
0342 B25       CC   J                                                      PCIR 
0343           A    *-6,LINECT                                             PCIR 
0344           MLC  +SUBJ2,P05+3                           NAME LINE       PCIR 
0345           B    P01                PRINT LINE                          PCIR 
0346 * SET PRINT ROUTINE TO PRINT SUBJECT CODE DETAIL LINE.                PCIR 
0347 B29       MLC  +DET2,P05+3                                            PCIR 
0348           B    P01                PRINT LINE                          PCIR 
0349           A    *-6,RECNT      ADD 1 TO RECORD COUNT.                  PCIR 
0350           A    *-6,SIREC   ADD 1 TO SUBJECT CODE DETAIL COUNT.        PCIR 
0351           B    B01                                                    PCIR 
0352 * BUILD PRINT LINE FOR MISSING DESCRIPTION TABLE CARD.                PCIR 
0353 B32       MLC  INP11,SUB2                                             PCIR 
0354           MLC  BLANKS+38,SUBID2                                       PCIR 
0355           MLC  'SUBJECT CODE TITLE CARD MISSING',SUBID2-38            PCIR 
0356           B    B25                                                    PCIR 
0357 *  INPUT OUT OF SEQUENCE                                              PCIR 
0358 B33       NOP  609                                                    PCIR 
0359           H                                                           PCIR 
0360           B    B33                                                    PCIR 
0361 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0362 *  MAIN ROUTINE - KEYWORD PROCESSING                                  PCIR 
0363 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0364 * BUILD KEYWORD INDEX PRINT LINE.                                     PCIR 
0365 B35       MLC  INP71,SERCH1        SEARCH KEYS                        PCIR 
0366           MLC  INP74,STC1          INSTALLATION CODE                  PCIR 
0367           MLC  INP79,ID1           PROGRAM I.D.                       PCIR 
0368 * SET PRINT ROUTINE TO PRINT KEYWORD INDEX LINE.                      PCIR 
0369           MLC  +DET1,P05+3                                            PCIR 
0370           B    P01                PRINT LINE                          PCIR 
0371           A    *-6,RECNT      ADD 1 TO RECORD COUNT.                  PCIR 
0372           A    *-6,KWREC   ADD 1 TO KEYWORD INPUT COUNT.              PCIR 
0373           B    B01                                                    PCIR 
0374 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0375 * READ HEADER LABEL                                                   PCIR 
0376 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0377 H01       SBR  H99+3                                                  PCIR 
0378 H02       RWD  1                                                      PCIR 
0379 H02J      RT   1,INPUT                                                PCIR 
0380           SBR  *+4                                                    PCIR 
0381           MLZS 0                   DECREMENT TO GM POS.               PCIR 
0382           MLC  ' '                 BLANK OUT I.R.G GM.                PCIR 
0382B          MLCWA'⯒',GM    GMWM TO INPUT AREA DEFINING POINTS.          PCIR 
0382C          MLCWA'⯒'                                                    PCIR 
0382G          BEF  H15                                                    PCIR 
0383           BER  H02J1                                                  PCIR 
0385           C    INPUT+3,'1HDR'      IS IT A HEADER-                    PCIR 
0386           BU   H12                 NO                                 PCIR 
0387           C    INPUT+22,'SIR'      SIR SHOULD BE REEL I.D.            PCIR 
0387C          BU   H13                                                    PCIR 
0388           C    INPUT+18,H02CT      CHECK REEL SEQ. NUMBER             PCIR 
0388C          BU   H14                                                    PCIR 
0389 H02JC     A    '1',H02CT           OK-ADD 1 TO REEL COUNT.            PCIR 
0390 H02J3     S    H02K4               CLEAR ERROR COUNTER.               PCIR 
0391 H99       B    XXXX                EXIT.                              PCIR 
0392 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0393 *   ERROR CONDITION   -  HEADER LABEL                                 PCIR 
0394 H02J1     A    *-6,H02K4           ADD 1 TO ERROR COUNTER.            PCIR 
0395           BCE  H02J2,H02K4,I       BR IF 9TH RETRY.                   PCIR 
0396           B    H02                 TRY AGAIN.                         PCIR 
0397 H02J2     S    H02K4               CLEAR ERROR COUNTER.               PCIR 
0399 H06       NOP  578                                                    PCIR 
0400           H                                                           PCIR 
0401           B    H02                                                    PCIR 
0402 *                                                                     PCIR 
0403 H02K4     DCW  +0                  ERROR COUNTER.                     PCIR 
0404 H02CT     DCW  '001'         REEL COUNT                               PCIR 
0405 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0406 * INCORRECT REEL OR NO HEADER LABEL.                                  PCIR 
0407 H12       NOP  566                NO HEADER LABEL HALT                PCIR 
0407B          H                                                           PCIR 
0407C          BSP  1                                                      PCIR 
0407D          B    H14S                                                   PCIR 
0408B*******************************************************************   PCIR 
0408CH13       NOP  567            SIR NOT I.D. ON HEADER LABEL            PCIR 
0408D          H                                                           PCIR 
0408E          B    H14S                                                   PCIR 
0409A*******************************************************************   PCIR 
0409BH14       NOP  568       INCORRECT REEL SEQUENCE NUMBER HALT.         PCIR 
0409C          H                                                           PCIR 
0409DH14S      BSS  H02JC,E   BRANCH TO IGNORE CONDITION AND CONTINUE  -   PCIR 
0409E          B    H02       OR - MOUNT PROPER REEL AND CONTINUE.         PCIR 
0409I*******************************************************************   PCIR 
0409J* A TAPE MARK IS THE 1ST RECORD ON THE SIR FILE - MOUNT PROPER        PCIR 
0409K* REEL AND PRESS START.                                               PCIR 
0409LH15       NOP  579                                                    PCIR 
0409M          H                                                           PCIR 
0409N          B    H02                                                    PCIR 
0410 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0411 * READ INPUT                                                          PCIR 
0412 *******************************************************************   PCIR 
0413 I01       SBR  I99+3              SET UP EXIT                         PCIR 
